          {"kind":"spacer","id":"gap-2","height":18},
          {"kind":"link","id":"crumb","text":"Help Center","url":"http://whatsapp.com/help"},
          {"kind":"heading","id":"h","text":"How to link a device","level":1},
          {"kind":"text","id":"t","text":"Linked devices let you use WhatsApp on up to four computers, tablets or phones at once, without keeping your phone online."},
          {"kind":"heading","id":"h-2","text":"Link a computer","level":2},
          {"kind":"text","id":"t-2","text":"1. Open WhatsApp Web or the desktop app on the computer; it shows a QR code. 2. On your phone, open WhatsApp, tap Settings (iPhone) or the three dots (Android), then Linked Devices, then Link a Device. 3. Unlock your phone if asked and point the camera at the QR code."},
          {"kind":"heading","id":"h-3","text":"Link with a phone number instead","level":2},
          {"kind":"text","id":"t-3","text":"On the computer, choose \"Link with phone number\", enter your number, and type the eight-character code it gives you into your phone under Linked Devices."},
          {"kind":"heading","id":"h-4","text":"Link a second phone","level":2},
          {"kind":"text","id":"t-4","text":"Install WhatsApp on the second phone, tap the three dots on the registration screen and choose \"Link to existing account\". Then scan its QR code with your main phone."},
          {"kind":"heading","id":"h-5","text":"Good to know","level":2},
          {"kind":"text","id":"t-5","text":"Linked devices stay signed in for 14 days without your phone connecting. Messages and calls stay end-to-end encrypted. Log out of a device from the Linked Devices list at any time."},
          {"kind":"link","id":"web","text":"Open WhatsApp Web","url":"http://whatsapp.com/web"},
          {"kind":"link","id":"next","text":"Next: back up and restore","url":"http://whatsapp.com/help/backup-and-restore"},
